R['fail-closed'][2] = """**REFUTED as written (the injection does not make the store read-only for the product); a different, worse behaviour found.** `ALTER DATABASE exponetdb_control SET default_transaction_read_only = on` + terminating the 23 backends (21:10:25): **mutations kept succeeding** (plans created at t=2 s, 21 s, 64 s, 127 s; rows exist in `operations.plans`), because the Control Store opens write transactions with an explicit `BEGIN ... READ WRITE` (`packages/control-store/src/store.ts:158`), which overrides the database default. Single statements outside such a transaction (the heartbeat `UPDATE`, grant last-use) do fail with `25006` (`heartbeat.failed`, `oauth.grant_use_failed`, worker `dataread.tick_failed 25006` ~200/min, `maintenance.loop_failed`). Readiness: `/healthz/ready` 200 until t~32 s, then **503 on serve, worker and gateway** (`heartbeat_stale`, `workers no_live_worker`); `GET /installation/health` -> `down`. So the roles report not_ready (and in production serve would leave the proxy) while the worker's operations loop still writes. Recovery is not automatic: `ALTER DATABASE ... RESET` from a session of that database fails (`cannot execute ALTER DATABASE in a read-only transaction`: connect to `postgres`), and after the RESET (21:23:11) all three roles stayed 503 for 4 min 36 s because the pooled sessions kept the old default; only terminating the backends brought them back (ready 9 s later). New finding S6-2. See `fc2b` for the real read-only store (hot standby). Raw: `fc2.out`, `fc2-undo2.out`."""

