R['graceful-life'][4] = """**CONFIRMED (stateless, no per-session memory) and a finding: concurrency costs memory before the limiter answers.** One MCP access token (DCR public client, authorization code + PKCE, 6 read scopes), `tools/list` (a 99 KB answer): 1,000 concurrent requests from the same grant for 30 s = 31,953 requests, **709 x `200`, 31,244 x `429 RATE_LIMITED`** (JSON-RPC `-32600 "Rate limited: retry after the time in Retry-After."`, `data.code RATE_LIMITED`, `retryAfterSeconds 1`; metric `exdb_mcp_denied_total{reason="rate_limited"} 31244`), latency p50 0.9 s, p99 3.3 s, max 6.2 s, no socket errors. `serve` RSS **156 -> 583 MB** (peak at 30 s), 1,080 open file descriptors (about one per connection), `/healthz/live` answered in 12-28 ms throughout (the event loop kept up); 10 s after the load RSS was 229 MB and fds 35. `deployment.md` §2a gives the serve container **512 MiB** (heap 259 MiB): this load would have been killed by the kernel here (no cgroup limit on the stack). `targets_list` 400 requests at concurrency 20: 118 x 200, 282 x 429 in 1 s (read class 20/s, burst 100 per grant). There is no session table, so "memory per session" does not exist; the memory is per in-flight request. An **unauthenticated** flood of the same shape (the first attempt, expired token): 86,471 x `401 UNAUTHENTICATED` in 30 s, RSS 182 -> 325 MB, fds ~1,700, `/healthz/live` 0.1-0.4 s. 1,000 distinct grants were not minted (one grant, one limiter bucket); the per-grant stream limit (4) was not exercised. Raw: `gl-mcp.out`."""

